# **Part 19. Five engineering principles to remember**

These are the principles that will make the biggest difference when designing your AI products.

**1. Never confuse a prompt with an application.**

A prompt is an instruction. An application is a complete execution system.

**2. Never let an AI model own your business rules.**

Use deterministic backend logic for permissions, constraints, billing, validation and execution limits.

**3. Never tie your entire architecture to one AI provider.**

Use provider adapters and standardized internal interfaces.

**4. Never assume an API success means a quality success.**

Evaluate the output against actual user requirements.

**5. Never make the system unnecessarily autonomous.**

Give agents bounded tools, explicit permissions, spending limits and human approval where appropriate.

